Gribbit, a gnome warlock with a penchant for purple robes and oversized goggles, whistled merrily as his succubus, Lilith, flitted around him in Stranglethorn Vale.  They were on the hunt for a rare jungle serpent, its scales rumored to be potent ingredients for a new potion. Lilith, with her seductive charm, easily distracted the local wildlife, allowing Gribbit to sneak up and cast his spells.  He chuckled as a particularly grumpy boar charged at Lilith, only to be ensnared by her Lash of Pain.  "Good girl, Lilith," he praised, "You're a real lifesaver."

**Answer:** Voidwalkers were more popular in Classic WoW because they provided better tanking capabilities, especially in group content, due to their taunt and sacrifice abilities. 


